WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.460
- If you live in Southern California

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.690
and you wear a hijab, make sure
you pin that (bleeps) down,

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.230
especially during Santa Ana season

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.850
'cause those winds will get you.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.710
- So, one day in college,

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:13.950
my friend was in the kitchen

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.130
and she was cooking something.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.210
Well, I was in the shower, do, do, do,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.930
just bathing away, and all I know is

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.790
the next thing that happened is,

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:24.740
"Get out, everything's on fire."

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.350
I think she forgot to turn off the stove.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.040
Kitchen was on fire, the roof was on fire,

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.080
and all I had on was nothing.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.570
But, I had to rush out
because the fire department

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.250
was already at the scene
and I put on a towel,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.230
no hijab, and just rushed out.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.130
I'm outside, then, trying
to just put on any layer

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.880
of clothing that my friends managed

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.730
to bring outside the house
as people are talking to us.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.900
All I have is a bunch of
firemen coming up to me,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.030
saying, "Are you guys okay?

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.090
"Are you okay, ma'am?",

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.960
and I'm like, "Yeah, I'm totally fine,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.480
"but please, just don't
look at me, I'm naked."

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.240
For all of you who think that we shower

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.780
with these things on, no, we
don't shower with our hijabs on

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.440
because I would have been
ready for that moment.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.940
- A few friends and I were
visiting San Francisco

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.970
to sight-see while we were in college.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:08.803
We had a great trip,

00:01:08.803 --> 00:01:10.100
and we were on our way
back to the airport.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.850
It was all going super smoothly

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.440
until we went to the TSA line,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.130
which is the most dreaded
part for every Muslim.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.030
So, we got in line, waiting
for it to be our turn,

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.500
and all of a sudden, one of
the security guards pointed

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.220
to what we thought were me and my friend,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.700
and said, "Ma'am, you
need to take that off,"

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.560
and we thought he was
talking about our hijabs,

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.170
so we went off, we were like,

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.480
"I'm calling my lawyer."

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.060
We didn't have lawyers.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.070
We were like, "You can't do this to us,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.280
"we know our rights.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.680
"We're Americans and this is America, sir,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.190
"so we're not gonna stand for that,"

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.510
and he waited for us to finish,

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.160
like, literally waited for
us to finish and was like,

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.310
"I was talking to your friend behind you

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.740
"because she forgot to take off her coat

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.990
"for security check.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.090
"Was not talking to you."

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.300
So, we awkwardly were like, "Oh.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.350
"Yeah, no, we knew that,

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.110
"we were just seeing if you knew that.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:58.943
"Bye."

00:01:58.943 --> 00:02:01.760
We basically just wasted 15
minutes of this guy's life,

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.340
preaching about equal rights
and freedom of religion,

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.480
for basically no reason.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.810
I guess the moral of the story is,

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.900
if you're gonna pick a fight with a TSA,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.390
just, like, maybe like,
look behind you first?

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.320
- So, I grew up in Southern California

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.340
and we have really strong winds every year

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.410
called the Santa Anas.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.710
These winds come and they
just blow everything away,

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.200
and one day in eighth grade,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.130
I was just minding my
own business at school

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.500
and the Santa Anas hit.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.460
This strong gust of wind,
it felt like a tornado,

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.280
it came and was just blowing
everything in the air.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.700
There was, like, leaves and dirt.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.680
Before I could even
register what happened,

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.610
the wind came and just attacked me,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.090
and my scarf flew completely off my head,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.060
and I just watched it fly away,

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.480
all the way across the quad.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.830
I chased it down for
maybe, like, 100 feet,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.550
and grabbed it really quick, I was like,

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.160
"Oh my god, this is crazy.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.610
"Everybody's gonna see me,"

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.750
and I just wrapped it
around and I looked up,

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.100
and everybody had just run away

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.450
and they were shielding their eyes

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.200
because there was so
much debris in the air,

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.860
so no one even saw, but it was, like,

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.630
the most mortifying 45 seconds of my life.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.370
In the moment, what seems like something

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.650
that's just so tragic and embarrassing,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.810
in the grand scheme of things,

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.100
it's not that big of a
deal and no one cares.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.330
- My story starts a couple months

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.820
after I started wearing my hijab.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.300
I was waiting in line in Six Flags

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.420
for one of my favorite rides, Tatsu.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.070
I'm the type of person
who loves rollercoasters,

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.980
but I can't put my hands in the air,

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.880
I have to hold on for dear life.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.940
We were sitting in Tatsu
and I was really excited,

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.190
and I was holding onto him like,

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.660
"Okay, I'm ready for this ride,"

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.530
and while we were starting,

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.900
I was like, "Wait, I totally forgot

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.770
"that this one goes upside-down,"

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.150
and I was like, "Okay, but it'll be fine."

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.090
So, we're going up, and then
as we're coming to the loop,

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.710
I was like, "Oh no, I
feel my hijab slipping,

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:41.970
"like, I feel it slipping."

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.380
I'm like, "Do I hold on,
do I hold onto my hijab?"

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.810
I didn't know what to do,

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.370
and I actually decided that
my scarf wasn't important

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.310
at that time and I'm just gonna hold on

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:52.270
for my dear life.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:55.000
When we were in the loop, I saw my scarf,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.780
I felt it just fly off and I was like,

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.360
"Okay, well there that goes.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.050
"I'm still alive, though,
and that's all that matters."

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.530
As that was happening,
I heard someone say,

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:05.740
"I got it," and I thought,

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.140
"That's such a weird thing
to say on a rollercoaster,

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.250
"why would you say that?"

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.040
And then, the ride ended,
and I was fine and alive,

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.540
I just didn't have the scarf on.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.710
I was like, sitting there, thinking,

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.390
"Should I put my shirt over my head?

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.040
"Like, how do I go about
the rest of my day?",

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.740
and the guy who was behind me yells again,

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.080
"I got it," and I turned around,

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.730
and I'm like, "What
are you talking about?"

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.420
I saw my scarf in his hand.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.940
He caught my hijab mid-air
on a rollercoaster,

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.773
who does that?

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:34.510
That was so sweet and kind of him,

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.390
and I could finally have something to wear

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.340
for the rest of the day.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.820
The moral of my story is,

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.960
if it comes between saving
my life or my hijab,

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.580
I'm gonna save my life.
(triumphant music)

